 Adding path amplitudes\n\nEach path carries a complex amplitude $a$ or $b$.\n\n$$P = |a + b|^2 = |a|^2 + |b|^2 + 2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$$", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 2}, {"id": "stream:practice-84c72011-3607-4b46-b67d-41846eab93f7", "role": "assistant", "text": "{\"questions\": [{\"question\": \"Two paths have amplitudes $1/2$ and $e^{i\\\\phi}/2$. Find $P(\\\\phi)$ and when it is zero.\", \"origin\": \"self_created\", \"source_refs\": []}]}", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 3}, {"id": "stream-user:branch:cross-term", "role": "user", "text": "Why is the cross term 2 Re(a* b)?", "concept_id": "paths", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 4}]}, "language": "en", "chapters": [{"id": "superposition", "title": "Superposition", "concept_ids": ["paths", "states"]}, {"id": "measurement", "title": "Measurement", "concept_ids": ["outcomes"]}], "learner_profile": {"goal": "Understand interference and measurement", "depth": "standard", "prerequisites": [{"topic": "Complex numbers", "level": "some"}], "focus": "Problem solving"}, "branch": {"id": "cross-term", "question": "Why is the cross term 2 Re(a* b)?", "selection": "a complex amplitude", "anchor": {"scroll_y": 240}, "restore_point": {"concept_id": "paths", "goal": "Predict interference", "next_step": "Start the lesson", "progress": ""}, "main_turn_id": "4ef635f9-7a86-4af8-b9c0-0db1481a8610", "selected_turn_id": "4ef635f9-7a86-4af8-b9c0-0db1481a8610", "selected_lecture": {"id": "4ef635f9-7a86-4af8-b9c0-0db1481a8610", "concept_id": "paths", "title": "Adding path amplitudes", "status": "completed", "text": "## Adding path amplitudes\n\nEach path carries a complex amplitude $a$ or $b$.\n\n$$P = |a + b|^2 = |a|^2 + |b|^2 + 2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$$", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-d54449110f1f8adcd8c2c8d4", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}]}, "turn_id": "branch:cross-term", "status": "unanswered", "decision": null, "choice": null, "created_at": 1795105962.3198838, "replies": [], "conversation": []}}, "attempt": 1, "status": "completed", "text": "Because $|z|^2 = z^* z$, the cross terms give $2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$.\n<teaching-decision>{\"depth\": \"short\", \"category\": \"local\", \"rationale\": \"Local algebra\", \"suggest_supplement\": false, \"supplement_goal\": \"\"}</teaching-decision>", "final_text": "Because $|z|^2 = z^* z$, the cross terms give $2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$.\n<teaching-decision>{\"depth\": \"short\", \"category\": \"local\", \"rationale\": \"Local algebra\", \"suggest_supplement\": false, \"supplement_goal\": \"\"}</teaching-decision>", "sequence": 3, "started_at": 1795105962.325591, "metrics": {"first_delta_s": 0.008676767349243164, "full_s": 0.020476341247558594, "save_s": 0.00013217000378062949}, "attempts": [], "resume_requests": []}');
